  "title": "New Object Context API & Breaking Changes Clarified",
  "summary": "Cloud Storage introduces a new `objects.viewFullContext` method to retrieve detailed object context, defined by the new `ObjectFullContext` schema. While the diff reports breaking changes, these apply to the required parameters of this *new* method, not existing API calls.",
  "details": "A significant update to Cloud Storage introduces the new `objects.viewFullContext` method. This method allows developers to retrieve comprehensive context information for objects, including extended data. It requires `bucket`, `object`, and `contextKey` parameters, with optional `generation` and `userProject`. The response is structured by the newly added `ObjectFullContext` schema, which includes fields like `createTime`, `updateTime`, `key`, `value`, `type` (with a `CUSTOM` enum), and a flexible `extendedData` object for arbitrary data.\n\nThe diff report indicates breaking changes related to `bucket`, `contextKey`, and `object` parameters becoming strictly required. However, these requirements are for the *newly introduced* `objects.viewFullContext` method. This means existing integrations and API calls are unaffected; developers integrating with this new method will simply need to ensure these parameters are provided from the outset. Minor internal adjustments were also made to the `Policy` schema's required permission annotations for `setIamPolicy` on objects and managed folders.",
  "impact": "medium",
  "breaking": true,
